    {
      "label": "ct:revealed-roots",
      "first_line": 462,
      "last_line": 464,
      "exact_statement": "\\begin{lemma}\\label{ct:revealed-roots}\nThere is a universal integer~$\\kappa\\geq30$ such that the following holds, with~$\\varepsilon$ as in Proposition~\\ref{fo:local-comparison}. Let~$K$ and~$\\gamma$ be as in Section~\\ref{rd:section}, with~$0\\in K$ and with a neighbor of~$0$ in~$\\gamma$, and let~$h\\geq10$ and~$r\\geq h^\\kappa$ be integers with~$\\diam_\\infty K\\geq16r$. Let~$A$ and~$\\Gamma$ be disjoint sets of vertices with~$K\\subset A\\subset K\\cup [-h,h]^2$ and~$\\gamma\\subset\\Gamma$. Then~$\\nu_{A,\\Gamma}\\bigl(\\cL(K\\cap [-3r,3r]^2)\\geq\\tfrac1{16}\\log r\\bigr)\\geq\\varepsilon/2$.\n\\end{lemma}",
      "statement_sha256": "1736377af34418a718d35c06ac69d33e33c4e488bffad2c7ea829a06cf4c1c33",
      "anchor": {
        "path": "FiniteAvalanchesFrozen/JointCofiniteV4.lean",
